    "prompt": "[Intro — spoken]\nLife can make a heart turn cold…\nPain can teach you not to trust.\nYou build walls so high\nyou forget how to let love in.\nBut Jehovah can reach a heart\nthat nobody else can touch.\n\n[Verse 1]\nBorn in the struggle, raised in the pain,\nCarrying burdens through the sun and the rain,\nToo young for the weight that was put on his back,\nToo young to understand why the world could be black.\n\nSaw his father angry, saw his mother cry,\nWatched the violence and wondered why.\nDeep in his heart, anger started to grow,\n“If I ever get older, I’ll make him know.”\n\nHe wanted a father who’d love him instead,\nBut hatred kept growing inside of his head.\nSo he ran from home, tried to run from the pain,\nBut wherever he went, that darkness remained.\n\nDrugs couldn’t silence the war in his mind,\nMoney couldn’t give him the peace he couldn’t find.\nHe asked God, “Why is life like this?”\nBut every road he took still ended in emptiness.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nWhen life makes you hard,\nyou learn how to hide.\nYou say, “I don’t need love,”\nwhile you’re breaking inside.\n\nBut a promise from Jehovah\ncan reach through the stone—\nAnd the heart you thought was dead\ncan finally come home.\n\n[Chorus]\nYou can change this heart of mine,\nJehovah, make me new.\nTake away the hate I’ve carried,\nteach my heart to trust in You.\n\n“Clothe yourselves with the new personality,”\nThat’s what Your Word can do.\nWhere there once was anger,\nlet compassion come through.\n\nThe past may have shaped me,\nbut it doesn’t have to own me.\nYour Word can break the chains\nand bring the lost back home to You.\n\n[Verse 2]\nThen came a message about justice to come,\nA Kingdom with no corruption, a government of One.\nA promise that the poor would no longer be crushed,\nThat the victims of violence would finally be touched.\n\nThe Bible said,\n“He will rescue the poor who cry for help,”\nAnd suddenly hope wasn’t something for somebody else.\nA peaceful earth—could it really be true?\nCould Jehovah make something beautiful new?\n\nHe started to listen, started to pray,\nStarted putting old habits and addictions away.\nHe knew if he wanted Jehovah to see,\nthe person he was couldn’t be who he’d always be.\n\n“Strip off the old personality,”\nThen “clothe yourselves with the new.”\nNot overnight—but day after day,\nJehovah’s Word started changing what pain had made.\n\n[Chorus]\nYou can change this heart of mine,\nJehovah, make me new.\nTake away the hate I’ve carried,\nteach my heart to trust in You.\n\n“Clothe yourselves with the new personality,”\nThat’s what Your Word can do.\nWhere there once was anger,\nlet compassion come through.\n\nThe past may have shaped me,\nbut it doesn’t have to own me.\nYour Word can break the chains\nand bring the lost back home to You.\n\n[Verse 3 — more emotional]\nThen came the hardest thing—\nthe man he couldn’t forgive.\nYears of pain saying,\n“How could you ever let this live?”\n\nBut the Bible kept working,\nslowly changing his view.\nIf Jehovah could forgive,\ncould he learn to forgive too?\n\nThe hatred he’d carried\nsince the days he was young\nstarted losing its power\none prayer at a time.\nThe walls started falling,\nthe anger released,\nAnd where there once was hatred,\nJehovah planted peace.\n\nThen father and son stood face to face,\nAfter all those years,\nafter all that pain.\nAnd for the first time in his life,\nhis father pulled him close.\n\nNo revenge.\nNo bitterness.\nJust a hug.\n\nSometimes the greatest miracle\nisn’t changing your past—\nit’s changing what your past\nmade you become.\n\n[Bridge — sung, building]\n“Let the peace of the Christ rule in your hearts.”\nLet it rule… let it rule.\n“Continue putting up with one another\nand forgiving one another freely.”\n\nJehovah didn’t erase the scars,\nHe taught the heart how to heal.\nHe didn’t change what happened,\nHe changed what the heart could feel.\n\n[Final Chorus — powerful]\nYou can change this heart of mine,\nJehovah, make me new.\nTake away the hate I’ve carried,\nteach my heart to trust in You.\n\n“Clothe yourselves with the new personality,”\nLet Your Word live inside.\nWhere there once was anger,\nnow there’s peace I cannot hide.\n\nThe past may have shaped me,\nbut it doesn’t have to own me.\nThe pain may have hardened me,\nbut You can make me soft again.\n\n[Outro — slow]\n“Let the word of the Christ reside in you richly…”\n\nSo let it live in me.\nLet it change me.\nLet it soften me.\n\nBecause I thought I needed revenge…\nwhen what I really needed\nwas Jehovah.\n\nAnd now when I look back,\nI don’t see the man I used to be.\n\nI see a heart\nthat Jehovah made new.",
