    "tags": "Rap",
    "prompt": "[Intro — spoken]\nI used to look at this world and say,\n“Somebody’s gotta make this right.”\nI carried anger like a weapon,\nThought I had to join the fight.\nBut then I opened up the Scriptures,\nAnd Jehovah showed me why—\nThe battle I was fighting\nWas never mine to win by force.\n\n[Verse 1]\nI saw the hurt, saw the tears, saw the people getting crushed,\nSaw the powerful take more while the innocent got pushed.\nEverywhere I looked, another reason to be mad,\nI wanted justice so badly,\nI thought violence was the path.\n\nI said, “If nobody saves us, then somebody has to stand.”\nSo I put my trust in movements made by imperfect man.\nBut the more I fought the darkness,\nThe more darkness filled my heart.\nI wanted to change the world,\nBut Jehovah changed my heart.\n\n[Pre-Chorus — melodic]\nThen I heard a different promise,\nSomething deeper than revenge:\nNot a temporary victory,\nBut a world where suffering ends.\n\n[Chorus — sung]\n“The meek will possess the earth,”\nAnd I finally understood—\nI don’t need to fight with hatred\nTo believe that justice could.\n“Let your Kingdom come,”\nThat’s the prayer I carry now.\nJehovah sees the brokenhearted,\nAnd He will make things right somehow.\n\nI thought I needed power,\nI thought I needed war—\nBut I found the fight worth fighting\nWas for Jehovah even more.\n\n[Verse 2 — faster rap]\nPsalm 72 showed me a King who won’t ignore the poor,\nWho doesn’t turn away the ones who’ve suffered at the door.\nNot ruling for himself,\nNot chasing fame or gold,\nBut bringing real relief\nTo the people left alone.\n\n“He will rescue the poor who cry for help,”\nThat’s the promise that I heard.\nNot a slogan from a movement—\nThat’s Jehovah’s own Word.\n\nAnd Jesus taught me something\nThat my anger never could:\n“Happy are the peacemakers,”\nNow I finally understood.\n\nI don’t have to hate my enemy\nTo stand for what is right.\nI can keep my conscience clean\nAnd still refuse injustice’s lie.\n\n[Pre-Chorus — melodic]\nI can’t repair this whole world,\nBut I know the One who can.\nAnd when Jehovah says He’ll fix it,\nI can trust His perfect plan.\n\n[Chorus — sung]\n“The meek will possess the earth,”\nAnd I finally understood—\nI don’t need to fight with hatred\nTo believe that justice could.\n“Let your Kingdom come,”\nThat’s the prayer I carry now.\nJehovah sees the brokenhearted,\nAnd He will make things right somehow.\n\nI thought I needed power,\nI thought I needed war—\nBut I found the fight worth fighting\nWas for Jehovah even more.\n\n[Bridge — quiet, emotional]\nOne day there won’t be crying.\nOne day there won’t be pain.\nOne day the ones who suffered\nWon’t have to hurt again.\n\nJehovah made a promise,\nAnd I hold onto His Word:\n\n“He will wipe out every tear from their eyes.”\n\nNo more begging for justice.\nNo more wondering why.\nThe King will bring the answer.\nAnd this time—\n\nIt will last.\n\n[Verse 3 — building]\nSo I put down the anger,\nBut I didn’t lose my voice.\nI found a stronger reason\nTo believe I made the choice.\n\nI can speak about the Kingdom,\nI can show somebody love,\nI can tell the brokenhearted\nThere’s a government above.\n\nNot built by human hands,\nNot controlled by human pride,\nBut Jehovah’s righteous Kingdom\nWith the Christ at its side.\n\nAnd when I see injustice,\nYeah, it still can make me hurt.\nBut I don’t have to become violent\nJust because this world’s absurd.\n\nI remember who I serve.\nI remember what He said.\nThe future isn’t hopeless—\nJehovah’s Kingdom lies ahead.\n\n[Final Chorus — full, emotional]\n“The meek will possess the earth,”\nNow I know what that means.\nNot another human struggle,\nNot another broken dream.\n\n“Let your Kingdom come,”\nThat’s the cry inside my heart.\nI wanted to change the world—\nJehovah showed me where to start.\n\nI thought I needed power,\nI thought I needed war.\nBut I found the fight worth fighting\nWas for Jehovah even more.\n\n[Outro — sung/spoken]\nI wanted justice.\nJehovah promised justice.\n\nI wanted peace.\nJehovah promised peace.\n\nI wanted a world without suffering.\nJehovah promised something better—\n\nA world where suffering\nwill be no more.\n\nSo I won’t lose hope.\nI won’t give in to hate.\nI’ll keep preaching the Kingdom\nAnd patiently wait.\n\nBecause the fight I was looking for\nWas never fought with fists.\n\nIt was faith.\nIt was love.\nIt was Jehovah’s Kingdom.",
