    "prompt": "[INTRO]\nWhen the innocent cry,\nWhen the helpless fall,\nWhen the prison doors close,\nJehovah hears us all.\n\nJehovah sees.\nJehovah hears.\n\n[VERSE 1]\nThey said, “Be quiet,”\nThey said, “Obey.”\nBut faith kept shining\nThrough the darkest day.\n\nHands were tied,\nAnd bodies bruised.\nThey would not give up\nThe truth they knew.\n\nCold prison walls,\nA lonely night.\nStill they held on,\nStill they held tight.\n\nThough men brought pain,\nThough men brought fear,\nThey knew their God\nWas always near.\n\n[PRE-CHORUS]\nWho sees the tears\nWe hide away?\nWho hears the prayers\nWe cannot say?\n\n“Jehovah is close\nTo the brokenhearted.”\nWhen hope seems gone,\nHe stays beside us.\n\n[CHORUS]\nThey can hurt us,\nThey can break us,\nThey can lock us away.\nBut they can’t take\nThe faith we hold\nIn Jehovah’s name.\n\nThey can strike us,\nThey can shame us,\nThey can threaten our lives.\nBut Jehovah sees,\nJehovah hears,\nAnd He will stand by.\n\n[VERSE 2]\nThey speak of God,\nThey speak His name,\nBut men can twist\nThe truth for gain.\n\nSo search the Word,\nAnd you will find\nA God of justice,\nTrue and kind.\n\nNot human power,\nNot human fame,\nCan ever stand\nAgainst His name.\n\nThough kingdoms rise,\nThough kingdoms fall,\nJehovah’s purpose\nOutlives them all.\n\n[PRE-CHORUS]\nWho sees the tears\nWe hide away?\nWho hears the prayers\nWe cannot say?\n\n“Jehovah is close\nTo the brokenhearted.”\nWhen hope seems gone,\nHe stays beside us.\n\n[CHORUS]\nThey can hurt us,\nThey can break us,\nThey can lock us away.\nBut they can’t take\nThe faith we hold\nIn Jehovah’s name.\n\nThey can strike us,\nThey can shame us,\nThey can threaten our lives.\nBut Jehovah sees,\nJehovah hears,\nAnd He will stand by.\n\n[BRIDGE]\n“Many are the hardships\nOf the righteous one,”\nBut Jehovah rescues\nEvery single one.\n\nFrom the prison cell,\nFrom the deepest pain,\nHe can give us strength\nTo stand again.\n\nJehovah sees.\nJehovah hears.\nJehovah stays near.\n\n[BREAKDOWN — CALL AND RESPONSE]\nWho sees us?\n\nJEHOVAH!\n\nWho hears us?\n\nJEHOVAH!\n\nWho gives strength?\n\nJEHOVAH!\n\nWho do we trust?\n\nJEHOVAH!\n\n[VERSE 3]\nJesus showed us\nHow to endure.\nHe loved his enemies,\nHe kept himself pure.\n\nHe was God’s Son,\nHe did His will.\nHe trusted Jehovah,\nAnd trusted Him still.\n\nWe follow Jesus,\nWe walk his way,\nBut Jehovah alone\nIs the One we praise.\n\nWhen the world shakes,\nWhen the wicked rise,\nJehovah remains—\nOur refuge and guide.\n\n[FINAL CHORUS]\nThey can hurt us,\nThey can break us,\nThey can lock us away.\nBut they can’t take\nThe faith we hold\nIn Jehovah’s name.\n\nThey can strike us,\nThey can shame us,\nThey can threaten our lives.\nBut Jehovah sees,\nJehovah hears,\nAnd He will stand by.\n\n[FINAL CHORUS — BIG]\nThey can hurt us!\nThey can break us!\nBut they can’t break our faith!\n\nThey can lock us!\nThey can beat us!\nBut Jehovah knows our pain!\n\nMany are the hardships—\nBut Jehovah rescues!\n\nJehovah rescues!\nJehovah rescues!\n\n[OUTRO]\nJehovah sees.\nJehovah hears.\nJehovah stays near.\n\nWe will not fear.\nWe will not fear.\n\nWe put our trust\nIn Jehovah.\n\nJehovah hears.",
