    "prompt": "[Verse 1]\nI remember where I’ve been,\nEvery failure, every wrong,\nThere were times I thought my past\nWould follow me for long.\nBut Jehovah saw my heart,\nHe could see I’d turned around,\nAnd the mercy He has shown\nIs the reason I’m still standing now.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI can’t change what’s behind me,\nBut I know what I can do—\nGive Jehovah what I have\nAnd keep moving forward too.\n\n[Chorus]\nThere are things ahead,\nThere are things ahead!\nI won’t keep looking backward\nAt the things I should have left.\nJehovah has forgiven,\nAnd His mercy gives me strength.\nI’ll keep running toward the prize,\nI’ll keep moving on today!\n\n[Verse 2]\nPaul knew what regret could do,\nHe remembered who he’d been.\nHe had fought against the brothers,\nYet Jehovah let him in.\nNot because he earned it,\nNot because his past was small,\nBut Jehovah showed him mercy,\nAnd that mercy changed it all.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nSo he didn’t stay defeated,\nHe got up and served again.\nHe received the ministry\nAnd gave his best until the end.\n\n[Chorus]\nThere are things ahead,\nThere are things ahead!\nI won’t keep looking backward\nAt the things I should have left.\nJehovah has forgiven,\nAnd His mercy gives me strength.\nI’ll keep running toward the prize,\nI’ll keep moving on today!\n\n[Verse 3]\nIf my actions hurt another,\nI will do what I can do.\nI’ll apologize sincerely,\nI will try to make things new.\nThen I’ll leave the matter there,\nPut my strength into the work.\nJehovah knows the heart that changed;\nHe will never leave me hurt.\n\n[Bridge]\n“Though your sins are like scarlet,\nThey will be made as white as snow.”\nThose are words from my Creator—\nWords I need to let me go.\n\nHe doesn’t keep finding fault,\nHe doesn’t hold my sins forever.\nHis loyal love surrounds me,\nAnd He helps me stand up better.\n\n[Breakdown]\nI was looking back—\nNow I’m looking forward!\nI was weighed down—\nNow I’m moving onward!\nWhat I cannot change,\nI place into His hands.\nJehovah has forgiven—\nNow I know where I stand!\n\n[Final Chorus]\nThere are things ahead,\nThere are things ahead!\nI won’t keep looking backward\nAt the things I should have left.\nJehovah has forgiven,\nAnd His mercy gives me strength.\nI’ll keep running toward the prize,\nI’ll keep moving on today!\n\n[Final Chorus — Bigger]\nThere are things ahead!\nThere are things ahead!\nWith Jehovah right beside me,\nI have nothing left to dread.\nThrough Jesus, my Redeemer,\nI have hope that will not fade.\nI’ll keep serving my God Jehovah,\nAnd I’ll never turn away!\n\n[Outro]\nThe past is behind me,\nThe future lies ahead.\nJehovah has forgiven—\nSo I’ll move forward instead.",
