    "prompt": "[Verse 1]\nI spent my life searching,\nTrying to find my way.\nQuestions filled my heart\nThat wouldn’t go away.\nI knew about religion,\nBut something still was gone.\nI wanted something real,\nSomeone I could truly know.\n\nThen I opened up Your Word,\nAnd You opened up my eyes.\nThe truth I’d been searching for\nWas right before my eyes.\n\n[Pre-Chorus]\nI learned Your name, Jehovah,\nThe God who gave me life.\nAnd through Your Son, Christ Jesus,\nYou brought me into Your light.\n\n[Chorus]\nI found what I was looking for,\nI found Jehovah, my God.\nYou filled the empty places\nThat this world could never fill.\n\n“Draw close to God,”\nAnd You will draw close to me.\nNow I know the One I needed\nWas Jehovah, my God.\n\nI searched the whole world over,\nBut now I finally know—\nWhen I found Jehovah,\nI found where I belong.\n\n[Verse 2]\nYou taught me through Your Word\nWho You really are.\n“This means everlasting life,”\nTo know You, the only true God.\n\nJesus is Your chosen King,\nYour Son whom You sent.\nHe taught me how to come to You\nAnd honor Your great name.\n\nYour Word became my lamp\nWhen I could not see the way.\n“Your word is a lamp to my foot”—\nYou led me day by day.\n\n[Bridge — quiet]\nI wasn’t looking for riches,\nI wasn’t looking for fame.\nI was looking for my Father,\nAnd I found Him through His name.\n\n“Jehovah is near\nTo all those calling on him.”\nNow those words are real to me—\nI know where I belong.\n\n[Final Chorus — full]\nI found what I was looking for,\nI found Jehovah, my God.\nYou filled my heart with purpose,\nYou showed me who You are.\n\nYou gave Your Son, Christ Jesus,\nTo lead me back to You.\nAnd now my heart can finally say,\n“My Father, I know You.”\n\nI searched the whole world over,\nBut now I finally know—\nI wasn’t looking for another thing.\nI was looking for Jehovah.\n\nThe One who gave me life,\nThe One whose name I know,\nThe One I’ll serve forever.\n\nJehovah, You are my God.",
    "hook": "I spent my life searching, / Trying to find my way. / Questions filled my heart",
